        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, a 78-year-old female admitted on 20/10/1997 with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination confirmed significant airflow obstruction. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. She was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Continuous pulse oximetry monitoring was maintained throughout. She responded well to treatment with improvement in respiratory function. She is discharged home in stable condition. Please continue bronchodilator therapy and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>"
            },
